    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to students’ pace and style. They can explain concepts in relatable ways, like using art or music analogies. They offer instant feedback and reduce anxiety by breaking down problems. In classrooms, they could act as interactive tutors, especially for visual or creative learners like myself. But human guidance is still essential."
